WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.477
The gateway has power, but new readings stopped.

00:00:02.522 --> 00:00:04.900
Diagnose lets your AI investigate remotely.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.711
On site, connect the gateway by USB and start the probe.

00:00:08.756 --> 00:00:12.900
Choose permissions, then share the nine-letter invitation privately.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.158
Install the Diagnose skill once.

00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:20.900
In your agent, invoke it and paste the invitation with a description of the problem.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.763
Here, the user confirms the connection once.

00:00:23.808 --> 00:00:26.900
Tasks and results proceed under their chosen permission mode.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.342
An encrypted relay connects the computers.

00:00:29.387 --> 00:00:30.624
The probe is now reachable.

00:00:30.669 --> 00:00:32.900
The agent still needs to check the gateway.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:38.823
The gateway is sending readings on its current USB port, but the collector still uses the old port.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.900
The agent explains the mismatch.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.965
The site user agrees to update the collector's port.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.900
The agent records the old setting and applies the correction.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.539
A new gateway reading reaches the dashboard.

00:00:50.584 --> 00:00:54.900
The agent reports what changed and the user can review the local audit history.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.976
Try a manual session first.

00:00:57.021 --> 00:00:59.900
For repeat work, launch with a device procedure.
